WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.980
It was a night of celebrations for supporters
of France's new centrist party,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.600
La republic en Marche - Republic on the move.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.860
"My dear fellow citizens, France is back.

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:23.570
For a month the President of the Republic
has embodied confidence, will, and boldness,

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.610
in France as well as on the international
stage.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.710
The government on his side illustrates, through
its composition, a completely new grouping,

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.720
and it is determined to serve France and to
respond to the French people's expectations."

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.100
Pollsters predict that the party could win
400 or more seats out of 577 in Parliament,

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.930
after next Sunday's second round.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:55.640
A majority that will be crucial to push through
controversial reforms to work and pensions.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.100
But voter turnout was at a record low on Sunday
- and opponents from both sides of the political

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:08.000
spectrum say that means President Macron doesn't
have the mandate to carry out those reforms.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.140
Far right Front National leader Marine Le
Pen called on citizens to use their votes

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.360
to stop Macron's plans.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.579
"We need some real members
of parliament who will oppose the catastrophic

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:28.140
policies Emmanuel Macron is preparing.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.360
He is about to commit a slaughter of
labour laws that will send millions of workers

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.800
into instability without bringing anything
to companies."

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:42.080
There's also concern that a huge parliamentary
majority for La Republic En Marche would leave

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.840
little room for debate - as far left leader
Jean Luc Melenchon warned:

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:56.560
"In the second round, do not give and don't allow anyone to give total power to the president's party."

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.880
Politicians are now racing to get people to
the polls for next Sunday's run off.

